# Fixing a Hole, intro (figure 110.1)
# Harpsichord: a held top C over two inner lines, A G# Ab and F E Eb D, with Pollack's chord names
# (C-aug written Caug, B-flat 9 written Bb9). The intro is two and a half bars; his "2 beats"
# over the last bar is kept as a bar mark.
# Octaves: close position under the top C (C5 over A4 and F4).
#? The last bar is only two beats long but is played as a full bar: the format can't shorten one bar.
#? Pollack's "F9" over i7- reads as an f-minor seventh (F Ab C Eb in the voices); kept as he spells it.
key F

system
voice "Top"      | C5 | - | [2 beats] - |
voice "Middle"   | A4 G#4 | Ab4 | - |
voice "Middle"   | F4 E4 | Eb4 D4 | - |
chords           | F{I} Caug{V5+} | F9{i7-} Bb9{IV} | - |
